                <pb facs="0461" n="445" sameAs="frus:frus1947v04/pg445"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>The widely-publicized Krakow Trials in which 17 Polish citizens including a
                    leading official in the Polish Peasant Party were charged with maintaining
                    contacts with the underground and furnishing “espionage material” to
                    representatives of foreign powers ended on September 11. On September 18, the
                    Department of State issued a statement denying charges made during the trial
                    that former Ambassador Lane and members of his staff were among the chief
                    recipients of the alleged “espionage materials”. For the text of the
                    Department’s statement, see Department of State <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bulletin</hi>, October 5, 1947, page 706.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
